WEBVTT

00:46:26.197 --> 00:46:30.463
and letting the other improvements
not be offset by this.

00:46:31.263 --> 00:46:36.530
It'll be a source of great pride

00:46:36.563 --> 00:46:38.930
that, hey, we came together.

00:46:38.963 --> 00:46:40.797
Giussani: OK, let’s hope 
that we actually do.

00:46:40.830 --> 00:46:43.163
Bill Gates, thank you
for sharing your knowledge,

00:46:43.163 --> 00:46:45.297
thank you for this very,
very important book.

00:46:45.330 --> 00:46:47.563
And thank you for coming back to TED.

00:46:47.563 --> 00:46:49.697
I want to close by showing
another short clip

00:46:49.697 --> 00:46:52.397
from the TED-Ed animation series
inspired by Bill's book.

00:46:52.430 --> 00:46:55.763
This one is about material
that's all around us,

00:46:55.763 --> 00:46:59.163
has a big carbon footprint
and how to reinvent it.

00:46:59.563 --> 00:47:01.397
Now, the series includes seven videos.